ge 57 | Compensation: $3.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $294K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $66K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["SkyWest, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.0B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $908M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.20\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.9\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 0.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $15.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-15845737.52},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 80% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 60% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SkyWest (NASDAQ:SKYW) Sets New 52-Week Low After Analyst Downgrade","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/skywest-nasdaqskyw-sets-new-52-week-low-after-analyst-downgrade.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793934070.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Investors Heavily Search SkyWest, Inc. (SKYW): Here is What You Need to Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020393/investors-heavily-search-skywest-inc-skyw-here-is-what-you-need-to-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks_v1-3020393","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793624402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SkyWest (SKYW) Posted Q3 Growth But Cut Outlook, Is The Stock A Bargain?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.