urns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.85).","It converts 22% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.20x.","ROE of 16% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.7x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 6pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.5% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.7x net debt to EBITDA ($706.9M of cash against $2.4B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 5.9x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.70 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The current ratio of 0.65 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 10.5% over 3 years, 13.8% over 5 years and 2.7% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 13%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 7.9% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.0% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 13%.","Capex runs only 0.1x depreciation (0.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.4%, and institutions hold 98%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (12 sales, net $15.8M sold).","The share count has shrunk 5.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 13,818 employees, each generates about $294K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median.","That works out to $66K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.7M (12x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $1K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":68,"head":"Avoid: Altman Z in the distress zone (1.70).","pros":["Model r